data: {"type":"agent_chunk","agent":"analyst","content":"- **Core mechanism:** A guide RNA directs Cas9 to a specific DNA location, where the protein cuts the strand [1]. This cut is based on a bacterial antiviral defense system [7].\n\n- **Two editing strategies:** Researchers either knock out genes by breaking them or supply a repair template to replace a disease-causing mutation with a healthy sequence [3].\n\n- **Expanding uses:** The approach now extends to bacteria, as in CRISPR SWAPnDROP, which enables genome editing and large-scale DNA transfer between bacterial species using *E. coli* as a model [4]."}

